# Vivemar Astro Project Rules

Use these rules when editing the Vivemar Astro site.

## Project Shape

- This is an Astro 5 static site with TypeScript, content collections, sitemap integration, and project-local CSS.
- Keep pages in `src/pages/`, reusable UI in `src/components/`, layouts in `src/layouts/`, shared data in `src/data/`, content entries in `src/content/`, and global styles in `src/styles/global.css`.
- Prefer static generation and build-time data. Add client-side JavaScript only when the interaction genuinely needs it.
- Match existing Spanish naming and content tone unless the requested change explicitly changes language or market.

## Astro And TypeScript

- Use `.astro` components for presentational UI and page composition.
- Use `getStaticPaths()` for dynamic content pages and keep slug/data lookup logic simple and typed.
- Keep TypeScript strictness compatible with `astro/tsconfigs/base`; avoid `any` and prefer narrow interfaces near the data they describe.
- Import shared site data from `src/data/` instead of duplicating business facts across pages.
- Preserve the existing `@astrojs/sitemap` setup and `SITE_URL` environment override in `astro.config.mjs`.

## Styling

- Use the existing CSS system in `src/styles/global.css`, including CSS custom properties such as `--oceano`, `--teal`, `--arena`, `--laton`, `--radio`, `--serif`, and `--sans`.
- Do not introduce Tailwind, CSS frameworks, component libraries, or broad design-system rewrites unless explicitly requested.
- Favor semantic class names already present in the codebase and keep responsive behavior based on stable layout constraints.
- Maintain the quiet luxury coastal visual direction documented in the project styles and docs.

## Content, SEO, And Accessibility

- Real estate content should keep property/location facts consistent across content files, listing cards, and detail pages.
- Maintain useful page titles, meta descriptions, canonical-friendly URLs, semantic headings, and descriptive image alt text.
- Use the existing `public/img/` assets when they represent the property or place accurately.
- Keep forms, contact links, and WhatsApp flows accessible and resilient without JavaScript.

## Implementation Checks

- After meaningful changes, run `npm run build` from `vivemar`.
- Check generated routes for dynamic pages when editing content collections or slug logic.
- Do not edit `dist/` unless the task is specifically about generated output or deployment artifacts.
